@page "/"
@inherits home.HomeBase

<PageTitle>Typhon + Blazor WebAssembly</PageTitle>

<h1>Blazor WebAssembly with a Typhon code-behind</h1>

<p>
    Each page is a <code>.razor</code> file for the markup and a <code>.ty</code> file for the logic: the component
    inherits a Typhon class (<code>@@inherits counter.CounterBase</code>) and the markup uses its fields, properties
    and methods. The browser downloaded the .NET runtime and this app's assembly once; from now on the Python code
    runs here, on WebAssembly, and no server is involved.
</p>

<ul class="links">
    @foreach (var link in links)
    {
        <li><a href="@link.href">@link.title</a>: @link.text</li>
    }
</ul>

<p class="muted">Rendered in your browser at @rendered_at by @runtime (@platform).</p>
